model {
  extend basalt.clientConnection {
    metadata {
      constraint "Native token rotation owns a single shared exchange and ordered durable write independently of validation waiters. It relies on the server's persisted same-pair refresh replay; unknown results retain a persisted first-attempt timestamp and replay until the server's one-hour replay window has passed since it, across sleep, restart and Reconnect. After that, or on definitive authentication refusal, the connection requires sign-in. A connection that requires sign-in or was revoked answers local agents with an authentication refusal on HTTP and WebSocket, never a retryable one. Cancelling or restarting a validation waiter cannot discard a token response; explicit disconnect or sign-out fences late writes. The local gateway limits simultaneous connection starts, not active model or tool streams. Up to 1,024 authenticated starts wait in arrival order for at most thirty seconds before dispatch; overflow refuses with retryable unavailability. HTTP response headers, WebSocket upgrades and refused handshakes release start capacity on both direct and native tunnel transports. Cancellation removes queued work; connection controls and shutdown still stop every queued and active operation. A failure before dispatch remains retryable without replaying an uncertain model request. Listeners request a backlog of 511 pending connections; the operating system can clamp it, including the default macOS limit of 128. This is a connection burst limit, not an active-stream limit; the client never changes the system setting. Deployment instance count and provider account capacity remain independent."
    }
  }
}
